<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1996</h1><p class="ref-lede">1996 in world history: 12 events, 16 deaths, 1 work and 1 state founded. 190 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1992">1992</a><a href="/years/1993">1993</a><a href="/years/1994">1994</a><a href="/years/1995">1995</a><a href="/years/1996" aria-current="page">1996</a><a href="/years/1997">1997</a><a href="/years/1998">1998</a><a href="/years/1999">1999</a><a href="/years/2000">2000</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-13">13 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Gunman kills 16 children and their teacher at Dunblane</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Thomas Hamilton opened fire in the gym of Dunblane Primary School in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> before killing himself. Public campaigning led to a near-total ban on private handgun ownership in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-17">17 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">TWA Flight 800 explodes off Long Island</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A Boeing 747 bound for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> exploded minutes after take-off from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, killing all 230 on board. Investigators concluded that a spark had ignited fuel vapour in the centre wing tank.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-27">27 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Bomb explodes in Atlanta's Centennial Olympic Park</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A pipe bomb exploded during a concert at the Atlanta Olympics, killing one woman and injuring 111. Security guard Richard Jewell was wrongly suspected; Eric Rudolph later confessed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-13">13 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Tupac Shakur dies after a drive-by shooting</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Rapper Tupac Shakur died in Las Vegas aged 25, six days after being shot. One of hip-hop's best-selling and most influential artists, his murder long went unsolved.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-24">24 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Comprehensive Nuclear-Test-Ban Treaty opens for signature</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The CTBT, banning all nuclear explosions, opened for signature at the UN and was signed first by President Clinton. It has not entered into force, as key states have not ratified it.</p></div></li></ol></section>
